>>SOURCE FORMAT FREE
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. DATEUTIL.

*> Compute due date = base date (YYYYMMDD) + terms days.
*> Uses INTEGER-OF-DATE / DATE-OF-INTEGER.
*> LS-STATUS: 0 = ok, 1 = invalid base date

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-BASE-INT              PIC S9(9) COMP-5.
01  WS-RESULT-INT            PIC S9(9) COMP-5.
01  WS-BASE-DATE             PIC 9(8).

LINKAGE SECTION.
01  LS-BASE-DATE             PIC 9(8).
01  LS-TERMS-DAYS            PIC 9(3).
01  LS-DUE-DATE              PIC 9(8).
01  LS-STATUS                PIC 9.

PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LS-BASE-DATE
                          LS-TERMS-DAYS
                          LS-DUE-DATE
                          LS-STATUS.
MAIN-LOGIC.
    MOVE 0 TO LS-STATUS
    MOVE ZERO TO LS-DUE-DATE
    MOVE LS-BASE-DATE TO WS-BASE-DATE

    IF WS-BASE-DATE IS NOT NUMERIC
        MOVE 1 TO LS-STATUS
        GOBACK
    END-IF

    IF WS-BASE-DATE < 16010101 OR WS-BASE-DATE > 99991231
        MOVE 1 TO LS-STATUS
        GOBACK
    END-IF

    COMPUTE WS-BASE-INT = FUNCTION INTEGER-OF-DATE(WS-BASE-DATE)
    IF WS-BASE-INT = 0
        MOVE 1 TO LS-STATUS
        GOBACK
    END-IF

    COMPUTE WS-RESULT-INT = WS-BASE-INT + LS-TERMS-DAYS
    COMPUTE LS-DUE-DATE = FUNCTION DATE-OF-INTEGER(WS-RESULT-INT)
    GOBACK.

END PROGRAM DATEUTIL.
